                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "49f99d49-968d-3337-bafc-20be0045f67e",
                        "entry_id": "1e04bf91-f3dc-39ef-be7c-bb4d779d71b6",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Qui diminue, qui va en arrière."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "88359ee7-7e56-44e3-867d-b31f7d0d2ecd",
                                "sense_id": "49f99d49-968d-3337-bafc-20be0045f67e",
                                "text": "Des intervalles récessifs."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "841952a4-8b6c-3279-921d-51e2049d621e",
                        "entry_id": "1e04bf91-f3dc-39ef-be7c-bb4d779d71b6",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Qualifie un gène qui ne s’exprime pas."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Génétique"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "895b8921-3c3e-4e17-a439-f57d432d427b",
                                "sense_id": "841952a4-8b6c-3279-921d-51e2049d621e",
                                "text": "Les géniteurs de résistance au froid : « Champagne » et « Austria Winter » renferment le plus grand nombre de gènes récessifs. Les pois d'hiver actuels en possèdent moins et les pois de printemps en sont pratiquement dépourvus."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "cb4825f0-1421-4007-8e01-c99ee3e6eec5",
                                "sense_id": "841952a4-8b6c-3279-921d-51e2049d621e",
                                "text": "Les phénotypes exprimés par les caractères récessifs ne s’embarrassent pas de frontières."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3ec287d9-5561-4a36-9298-3872bb3cf592",
                                "sense_id": "841952a4-8b6c-3279-921d-51e2049d621e",
                                "text": "Les fièvres récurrentes héréditaires constituent un groupe de maladies auto-inflammatoires rares de transmission autosomique récessive ou dominante."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "75ccb00a-de64-41e5-a513-664493718d23",
                        "source_entry_id": "1e04bf91-f3dc-39ef-be7c-bb4d779d71b6",
                        "target_lang_word": "recessive",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "recessive",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9cbd9429-e3a7-323a-bf5b-0d00407806bf",
                                        "entry_id": "e2cebe7b-4280-3f05-88c2-8923addeb620",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Going back; receding."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "442b1532-6dcd-339b-99c7-74351fb52b6a",
                                        "entry_id": "e2cebe7b-4280-3f05-88c2-8923addeb620",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Able to be masked by a dominant allele or trait."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "54e86902-2dd9-4877-8698-6c0a5ceb16c0",
                                                "sense_id": "442b1532-6dcd-339b-99c7-74351fb52b6a",
                                                "text": "1944 June 21, James A. G. Rehn, South African Bird-Locust Records and Notes (Orthoptera; Acrididae; Cyrtacanthacridinae; Group Cyrtacanthacres), Notulae Naturae, Number 137, Academy of Natural Sciences of Philadelphia, page 3,\nThe Lydenburg male and the other two females have the infuscate pattern definitely more recessive and less evident, although traceable."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1985ac81-8ff3-4563-8ed8-2a9f9d2d6436",
                                                "sense_id": "442b1532-6dcd-339b-99c7-74351fb52b6a",
                                                "text": "This plan takes advantage of the fact that barless is the most recessive of a series of alleles."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a3241068-f677-4c56-85c7-d2257ce2adca",
                                                "sense_id": "442b1532-6dcd-339b-99c7-74351fb52b6a",
                                                "text": "The series of murine Agouti alleles is a consistent array as it progresses from the most recessive to the most dominant allele (Jackson, 1994)."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "69f47575-8010-3436-ab0c-36b4fb6be7e9",
                                        "entry_id": "e2cebe7b-4280-3f05-88c2-8923addeb620",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Not dominant; whose effect is masked by stronger effects."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "51298bd1-3474-4988-91ef-7d33b6158319",
                                                "sense_id": "69f47575-8010-3436-ab0c-36b4fb6be7e9",
                                                "text": "The worker–client relationship is more recessive and has a more catalytic and enabling quality."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "21f0b30f-fa9c-482e-98a4-e80c931dfa7e",
                                                "sense_id": "69f47575-8010-3436-ab0c-36b4fb6be7e9",
                                                "text": "The law-making or legislative component was the most recessive component of the legal system of hunter-gatherers, although decisions or advice given by mediators were remembered and used again to settle similar violations of rules or disputes among parties."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "recessive",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6a943922-fd3c-39cc-8edb-f0a8c7d9a085",
                                        "entry_id": "437d3ceb-eee5-3146-83aa-ac76ffcbb95c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A gene that is recessive."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "271b2611-bd65-46d7-b1e1-6ca0bc4ecb68",
                                                "sense_id": "6a943922-fd3c-39cc-8edb-f0a8c7d9a085",
                                                "text": "Suppose, for example, that we started with a population consisting of pure dominants, heterozygotes, and recessives in the ratio 1 : 4 : 4."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "46eb1c8b-1c16-4196-ba67-36cd19432df3",
                                                "sense_id": "6a943922-fd3c-39cc-8edb-f0a8c7d9a085",
                                                "text": "Finally, if we suppose provisionally that the mutant genes are dominant just as often as they are recessive, selection will be far more severe in eliminating the disadvantageous dominants than in eliminating the disadvantageous recessives."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fa55d4e8-5827-463a-8028-35e7e2e3ceb5",
                                                "sense_id": "6a943922-fd3c-39cc-8edb-f0a8c7d9a085",
                                                "text": "Selection favoring recessives is common in maize breeding for several traits, such as sweetness, opacity, brachysm, lack of ligules."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "88b70c14-3eda-47f4-9d4a-14f2d249bb74",
                                                "sense_id": "6a943922-fd3c-39cc-8edb-f0a8c7d9a085",
                                                "text": "2008, Ascertainment Test, entry in George P. Rédei, Encyclopedia of Genetics, Genomics, Proteomics, and Informatics, page 147,\nIn three-child families 27/64 will have no affected offspring, 9/37 will have 2, and 1/37 are expected to have 3 recessives."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
